 "why_three_metrics": "any@3 is only correct where a question has ONE gold session. knowledge-update always has two (the original and the update) and multi-session has two to five, so on those any@3 scores retrieving one of several as a hit. For supersession that is inverted: returning only the original IS the stale answer this product exists to prevent.",
 "why_stratified": "the first run took data[:50] and every question was single-session-user, because the file is ordered by type. multi-session (cross-session) and knowledge-update (supersession) were zero of zero.",
